    fix(worker): make the once-per-turn error election atomic

    Claim an in-flight slot before the first await in signalError. errorSignalled
    is set only AFTER delivery (deliberately, so a failed first send cannot
    permanently suppress the terminal error), which means it could not elect a
    winner on its own: two overlapping callers both read it as false and both
    posted a user-facing error. The claim is released when delivery fails so a
    later signal can still retry.

